Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?Connect=20the=20analysis=20plan=20to=20Resu?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lts=20=E2=86=92=20Data=20Analytics:=20view,=20edit,=20apply?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The plan written in Intelligent mode (research.analysisPlan) was only shown
there; Data Analytics offered a one-shot "Create the planned analyses" copy
with no way to see, edit or re-sync it. Data Analytics now has an Analysis
plan workspace (overview, hypotheses, cross-tabs, tests, variables, charts,
themes & insights, reports, dashboards) reading the plan from the survey,
editing it through the engine's own analysis actions (new: update_crosstab,
update_analysis_test, reorder_analysis_plan) saved with the revision guard,
and an idempotent "Apply analysis plan" that keeps one saved analysis, chart
and dashboard widget per planned id, runs on real responses only when they
exist, maintains one findings report, and records each apply (migration 0050).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Hr35SrsN44edhJ8Z6mmA87
